  "findings": [
    "Inspected tables have eight distinct columns. Company names, category codes and wrapped category labels must be extracted by their own cells; non-manufacturing subclass cells can be blank.",
    "All seven PDF metadata creation dates precede or match their catalogue dates. Some older documents use a 202603 URL directory; that directory alone does not date the classified facts. Neither PDF metadata nor a current download proves exact historical publication time.",
    "The collected classification guideline contains only its first chapter. A full primary-source rule is still needed to establish the taxonomy and interpretation.",
    "Industry affects model features, residual targets, prediction neutralization, model gates, allocation, execution limits, manual-account validation and independent accounting checks. A feature-only change would leave inconsistent risk grouping.",
    "The statistical period in a table title is not its public availability date. Historical use needs a registered, conservative availability convention with no future-quarter backfill.",
    "CAPCO categories differ from the current metadata taxonomy. Taxonomy replacement and dated availability need separate attribution; no classification level is selected by backtest profit."
  ],
